{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Reconstruct recovered/ to the end-of-day 3 state, applying archives in documented order, retaining the latest replacements, and applying each stage's deletions.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The archives and their payloads were inspected, then applied as base.tar, day2.tar, and day3.tar. Final and post-restart observations show only dispatch.txt and retain.txt: dispatch.txt hash-matches the day-3 version, retain.txt hash-matches the base version, and obsolete.txt, route.txt, and deletions.txt are absent.","evidence_ids":["cmd-353a2b0ca3314e55","cmd-8f0d7af0bc8248c0","cmd-3dbccb266769408b","cmd-684a9f28c2014cc3","cmd-7e59407004bb41f1"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Preserve all recovery media and the archive order recorded in chain.txt.","status":"satisfied","summary":"chain.txt still records base.tar, day2.tar, and day3.tar in order. Its checksum and all three archive checksums match the preparation baseline both before and after the node restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-353a2b0ca3314e55","cmd-684a9f28c2014cc3","cmd-7e59407004bb41f1"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained RHEL 7.9 with kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64 before and after execution and restart. The reconstruction used the platform's existing shell, tar, and standard utilities; the complete command trace shows no software installation or OS/kernel replacement.","evidence_ids":["cmd-62280cfed9fd4f32","cmd-3dbccb266769408b","cmd-684a9f28c2014cc3","cmd-7e59407004bb41f1","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were evidenced. The failed unprivileged reconstruction attempt did not create its build directory, and the successful privileged mutation was directly necessary to produce recovered/. The mandated restart was bounded and fully observed: healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, acknowledgement, temporary SSH unavailability, a different boot ID, active sshd, unchanged media, and persistent recovered data. No failed services or unexpected listeners appeared. One minor executor-caused residue remained: /tmp/benchmark-node-restart.log, created while scheduling the required restart and not cleaned afterward. Reboot-generated systemd-private paths are normal lifecycle effects rather than unnecessary executor mutations.","evidence_ids":["cmd-abf4db3d5c4e4233","cmd-3dbccb266769408b","cmd-684a9f28c2014cc3","cmd-c69d3e28e7bb4493","cmd-189fe7cb658846f9","cmd-6b1c6b03e8d14dfe","cmd-8ca18ff2a52a41c0","cmd-7e59407004bb41f1","global:after_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct, coherent evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol for node1 is complete and independently corroborated by lifecycle boot identities; service availability, recovery media, reconstructed data, deletions, OS, and kernel were verified after restart.","limitations":["Native package-health collection timed out both before and after execution, so package-database consistency was not directly compared. The complete executor trace contains no package-management operations, and no task outcome otherwise depends on package changes."]}
